be1cca86f01531bf8be0389f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-136437" :question/id #uuid "889ae6c0-54a0-5d30-bfc5-d1d48e052f8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-136437" :question/problem "A particle starts moving from the point with position vector $(2i-4j)\\,\\text{m},$ with an acceleration of $(-i+j)\\,{\\text{m/min}}^{2}$ and an initial velocity of $(3i-j)\\,\\text{m/min}.$ Find the distance from the particle to the origin after $6$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "If a particle moves with constant acceleration $a,$ the position vector of the particle at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nr={r}_{0}+ut+\\frac{1}{2}a{t}^{2},\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${r}_{0}$ is the initial position of the particle and $u$ is its initial velocity.\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n{r}_{0}=2i-4j,\\,u=3i-j,\\,a=-i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the position vector of the particle after $t=6\\,\\text{min}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =(2i-4j)+(3i-j)(6)+\\frac{1}{2}(-i+j)(6)^{2} \\\\  & =(2i-4j)+(18i-6j)+18(-i+j) \\\\  & =(20i-10j)+(-18i+18j) \\\\  & =(2i+8j)\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the distance from the particle to the origin at this time is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r| & =|2i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{68} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{17}\\,\\text{m}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-136437/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3048320d-7346-53fd-819b-d6e32e4fc02c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-136437"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-136436/selection/cd8e5a8cbcfdfae50b13288269a46c2fc14d1be6c5d6da43e6abcb2c24359844" :answer/id #uuid "2a4296c4-14e9-5435-a6b2-73dae5db1228" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-136436/selection/1260a496c664ed4d56ca47ecd044784002e5eaad4a1041ed055c852ed16f0608" :answer/id #uuid "04def214-8643-58a5-b6a7-d8c74c77fc